  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fellowships</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 1974, the Ireland Fellows Programme has brought promising individuals from ODA-eligible partner countries to study for a master&#x2019;s qualification at an Irish University or Institute of Technology. The programme is intended to build capacity in these countries while simultaneously extending Ireland&#x2019;s network of influence and improving familiarity with Ireland amongst a cohort with the potential to become influential in their home country. The programme offers selected students the opportunity to undertake a fully-funded one-year master&#x2019;s programme at a prestigious higher education institution (HEI) in Ireland. The award covers course fees, flights, and accommodation and living costs.</narrative>
  </description>
